From 0dde784bdda19c7468ce15eecd69e56d12f9d611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:40:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firewall: shared REAPER_HOOK front chains - fixed layer order
 Warden -> Gatekeeper -> rules engine

Closes backlog "[HIGH] Firewall layer ordering". Warden, Gatekeeper and the
rules engine each hooked their own chain with `-I <base> 1`, so the LAST
layer to apply sat on top (cold boot and every restart_firewall: reaper_fw).
reaper_fw is the only layer emitting terminal ACCEPT (user allow, zone
policy, egress defaults, DNAT companion); the other two only DROP/RETURN.
An ACCEPT inside a chain jumped from INPUT/FORWARD ends traversal of the
table, so one allow rule silently re-admitted every threat-feed / geo-
blocked source and every quarantined device. Same race on OUTPUT
(REAPER_FWO vs RW_SELF); the order changed with every restart_gk /
restart_rwarden / gkd self-heal.

- rc/reaper_hook.[ch]: reaper_hook_gen() writes /tmp/reaper/hook.sh once;
  it flushes REAPER_HOOK / REAPER_HOOK_F / REAPER_HOOK_O, appends a jump for
  each layer chain that EXISTS in the invariant order Warden (REAPER_WARDEN,
  RW_SELF) -> Gatekeeper (REAPER_GKI/GKF per -i, list from /tmp/gk/ifs,
  charset-gated) -> rules engine (REAPER_FWI/FWF/FWO), then re-pins one base
  jump per chain with delete-all-then-`-I 1` (never `-C || -I`: position-
  blind). Logs when GK chains exist without an interface list.
- Every layer's apply script calls hook.sh at its tail, so the order
  converges whichever service restarted. Direct `-I <base>` emissions
  removed: reaper_fw.c (filter), gatekeeper.c (GKF/GKI; nat + ebtables
  unchanged), rwarden.c (REAPER_WARDEN v4/v6, RW_SELF).
- Teardowns strip the front-chain jumps and STILL strip the pre-v2.6.2
  direct jumps (upgrade path). rwarden's single `-D` became loops (a raced
  apply could leave a duplicate that kept the chain referenced).
- firewall.c: reaper_hook_gen() before the three re-applies; start_gk /
  start_rwarden / start_reaper_fw also call it.
- gkd.c: the armed probe now asserts the REAPER_HOOK_F jump, not just chain
  existence (a lost jump with a live chain read "armed" forever).
- reaper_fw.c: rfw_hook_of() removed (unused).

Host-verified: hook.sh passes sh -n / dash -n / shellcheck; mock-iptables
dry-run confirms order, per-interface GK jumps, disabled layers skipped,
bad interface list rejected, duplicate base jumps all removed.

(cherry picked from commit b04dcf0ae0d59f8eef2349acd3ce01d84f88cfed)
